  "result": "I fixed it in `split_arg_string` in `src/click/shell_completion.py`. I haven't run the tests or tried it in a shell.\n\n**Cause:** `split_arg_string` uses Python's `shlex`, which by default treats `#` as the start of a comment. Everything from the `#` onward was dropped, so an argument like `foo#bar` was cut to `foo`. The completion logic then saw the wrong arguments.\n\n**Fix:** I set `lex.commenters = \"\"` so `#` is kept as an ordinary character.\n\nI didn't add a regression test. One in `tests/test_shell_completion.py` would be something like `split_arg_string(\"a b#c\")` returning `[\"a\", \"b#c\"]`. I can add it if you want.",
